    "status": "ok",
    "headline": "Collin County Power Backup Report",
    "summary": "Homes in Collin County face an elevated risk of long power outages. Records from the past 8 years since 2018 show a long outage about once every 10 years. In February 2021, 34% of homes in the county lost power. The longest-waiting tenth faced about 73 hours. In May 2024, 23% of homes in the county lost power. The longest-waiting tenth faced about 51 hours. One Core lasts about 16 hours in January. One Core lasts about 35 hours in November. Two Cores are suggested. Two Cores last about 32 hours in January. The 2 Cores cover 51% of past 12-hour-plus outage hours. Base confirms sizing at install.",
